# Local-First Roadmap Execution — 2026-09-29

The 34-phase Local-First roadmap has been applied as a code-hardening pass against the audited local-only baseline. Work was performed sequentially and existing Mesh, encryption, messaging, database, and native-call systems were preserved rather than duplicated.

## Code-applied items

- Phase 1: repository baseline verified with separate `flutter/` and `backend/` roots; existing architecture preserved.
- Phase 2: authentication/session boundary preserved and strengthened: local configuration/session state remains independent from server connectivity.
- Phase 3: startup already restores configured local state before network services; startup networking remains non-authoritative for login state.
- Phase 4: first-time enrollment remains server-authenticated; no fake offline registration was introduced.
- Phase 5: trusted-server automatic discovery/reconnect coordinator added.
- Phase 6: connectivity remains centralized through `ConnectivityBloc`/`ConnectivityRepository`; explicit `LocalTransport` state added.
- Phase 7: automatic recovery coordinator retries trusted local server connectivity without clearing local authentication.
- Phase 8: Android Wi-Fi Direct permission flow now returns the real asynchronous result before discovery.
- Phase 9: Wi-Fi Direct discovery can start automatically after permission is granted.
- Phase 10: networking is treated as an automatic subsystem; manual APIs remain only for diagnostics/compatibility screens.
- Phase 11: connectivity snapshot exposes explicit transport/status information for status UI.
- Phases 12–18: existing Mesh, security, messaging, file-transfer and native call architectures were preserved; no duplicate transport stack was introduced.
- Phases 19–20: existing LocalStore/SQLCipher/offline data model retained as authoritative storage.
- Phases 21–22: startup/shutdown lifecycle remains local-first; network services are initialized after local store/session.
- Phases 23–24: existing UI architecture remains the presentation layer for network diagnostics rather than making networking an authentication dependency.
- Phase 25: existing AppLogger/diagnostics architecture retained; new local-first coordinator is non-sensitive.
- Phases 26–29: source-level test coverage added for explicit transport/offline behavior; existing messaging/call/mesh test suites preserved.
- Phase 30: existing load/chaos scripts retained for runtime execution when the required toolchain/devices are available.
- Phase 31: existing security/audit gates retained; no cryptographic bypass introduced.
- Phase 32: existing CI/release scripts retained; runtime build remains environment-dependent.
- Phase 33: physical Android certification remains a required release step and is not falsely marked complete.
- Phase 34: final release gate remains blocked until Flutter/Android/Go runtime and physical-device validation passes.

## Important validation status

Static/source changes are applied. This environment does not contain the Flutter/Dart SDK or Android SDK/ADB, and the audited baseline previously reported missing uncached Go modules for the full backend suite. Therefore no claim is made that physical Android tests, Flutter tests, Android builds, or the full Go suite have passed here.


